# Site-level log policy for the Majadu handlers on api.qouver.com.
#
# The share code and the one-use websocket ticket are query parameters, and this
# access log is shared with every other application on the site. Production and
# the RC API are served from the same site block and write to the same log, so
# both families of prefixes have to be named: naming only /majadu/s/* writes
# live tickets into a file that outlives the link. cutover.sh refuses a
# Caddyfile, or an installed copy of this file, that names fewer.
#
# Install (cutover.sh does this in its preflight) as:
#   /srv/qouver/apps/majadu/caddy/log-share.caddy
#
# then replace the bare `log` statement of the api.qouver.com site block with:
#   import /srv/qouver/apps/majadu/caddy/log-share.caddy
#
# `log_skip` is a site-level directive and needs Caddy 2.8+; the host runs 2.11.
# The pre-2.8 spelling was only ever accepted as a subdirective of `log`, and
# 2.11 rejects it there with "unrecognized subdirective", so a copy that still
# carries the old spelling is a Caddyfile that will not load. `log_access` is
# the host's existing output and format snippet; keep its name so the other
# applications log unchanged.
@share path /majadu/s/* /majadu/ws/* /majadu-rc/s/* /majadu-rc/ws/*
log_skip @share
log {
	import log_access
}
